      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of H2L (0.03 mmol), Dy(acac)3·2H2O (0.03 mmol), CH3OH (3 mL), C2H5OH (5 mL), 1,2-ethanediol (5 mL) and CH2Cl2 (3 mL) was stirred for 6.0 h at room temperature under atmospheric conditions. The resulting solution was filtered and the filtrate was allowed to stand and concentrate at room temperature. Yellow block crystals suitable for single-crystal X-ray diffraction were obtained by slow evaporation of the filtrate for about two weeks. The CO3^2− bridge is formed by spontaneous capture/fixation of atmospheric CO2.",
